#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0064 expect=noViolation domain=DM
#note "FRESH (documents finding SD0064-F1's DM half). DM is NOT excluded by the authored Scope (only AP--/APRELSUB are), the rule EXECUTES, and every DM USUBJID is trivially a member of its own \$dm_usubjid set -> noViolation. This pins the behavioral-equivalence claim that leaving DM in scope (against the PMDA sheet's '-DM') changes nothing."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SEX     type=Char label="Sex"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | M
S1 | DM | 002 | F
